WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.120 --> 00:00:05.820
There's nothing quite like curling up on the
sofa and marathoning Netflix's fine film selection.

00:00:05.940 --> 00:00:09.900
these are just a few of the flicks that deserve
way more attention than they're getting.

00:00:10.980 --> 00:00:15.920
Part apocalyptic thriller, part family drama,
the Ellen Page- and Evan Rachel Wood-led Into

00:00:15.929 --> 00:00:20.130
The Forest is a compelling, unsettling movie
that never quite goes where the viewer thinks

00:00:20.130 --> 00:00:20.860
it's going.

00:00:20.900 --> 00:00:26.080
Deep inside a beautiful, remote forest, sisters
Nell and Eva live in a stately, window-covered

00:00:26.080 --> 00:00:29.100
home with their father, played by Callum Keith
Rennie.

00:00:29.160 --> 00:00:33.320
There's been a far-reaching collapse of the
national grid, but Nell and Eva continue to

00:00:33.320 --> 00:00:36.620
live their lives as best they can until the
power comes back.

00:00:36.940 --> 00:00:38.400
Spoiler alert: It doesn't.

00:00:38.540 --> 00:00:43.399
Time passes agonizingly, the food and supply
reserves dwindle, and some truly horrific

00:00:43.399 --> 00:00:49.170
things happen as Nell and Eva, far from civilization,
wonder if society has completely collapsed,

00:00:49.170 --> 00:00:51.420
and fight for the lives they once took for
granted.

00:00:51.420 --> 00:00:55.579
Eventually, they can't wait around anymore
and must fend for themselves by heading…

00:00:55.580 --> 00:00:56.360
into the forest.

00:00:57.340 --> 00:01:02.560
The occasional bad gig is a necessary stumbling
block for a young band paying its dues, but

00:01:02.560 --> 00:01:08.160
hear us out: Green Room isn't a Spinal Tap-esque
comedy about the indignities musicians face.

00:01:08.840 --> 00:01:09.940
"Let me call my cousin.

00:01:10.360 --> 00:01:11.620
I can get you guys a solid gig."

00:01:11.620 --> 00:01:12.120
"Where?

00:01:12.440 --> 00:01:12.960
Here?"

00:01:13.260 --> 00:01:14.080
"Scene's dead.

00:01:14.360 --> 00:01:15.720
You'd have to dip down closer to Portland."

00:01:16.100 --> 00:01:21.750
Instead, it's a claustrophobic, intense, and
at times horrific pulse-pounder about a regular

00:01:21.750 --> 00:01:27.590
punk band, whose members include Imogen Poots,
Alia Shawkat, and the late Anton Yelchin,

00:01:27.590 --> 00:01:31.880
who get waylaid and trapped in the "green
room," the backstage waiting area, of a concert

00:01:31.880 --> 00:01:32.380
venue.

00:01:32.620 --> 00:01:33.120
Surprise!

00:01:33.120 --> 00:01:37.580
It turns out the place is actually a Nazi
skinhead bar, and one of the musicians just

00:01:37.580 --> 00:01:40.860
so happened to catch a glimpse of the body
of a recently murdered woman.

00:01:40.920 --> 00:01:44.720
As a result, the bad guys hold the band hostage
until they can kill them.

00:01:44.720 --> 00:01:49.270
Their leader is the worst of all, portrayed
by a very much against-type Patrick Stewart.

00:01:49.270 --> 00:01:51.570
Needless to say, he steals the spotlight.

00:01:51.570 --> 00:01:54.310
Well, he steals it and he stomps it to pieces.

00:01:54.310 --> 00:01:58.830
It's an intense, compelling, low-budget horror
movie of a different stripe, and one from

00:01:58.830 --> 00:02:01.500
which not everyone gets out alive, or intact.

00:02:02.780 --> 00:02:07.760
Over the last decade or so, the Chinese film
industry has exploded, producing big movies

00:02:07.760 --> 00:02:09.810
on par with Hollywood blockbusters.

00:02:09.810 --> 00:02:14.489
And as the Western canon provides a rich history
of fantasy, take The Lord of the Rings, for

00:02:14.489 --> 00:02:19.680
example, so too does China with Novoland,
a sprawling, 30-book series written by multiple

00:02:19.680 --> 00:02:24.090
authors that concerns a made-up, quasi-medieval
and magical universe.

00:02:24.090 --> 00:02:28.460
Legend of the Naga Pearls marks Novoland's
auspicious U.S. streaming debut.

00:02:28.629 --> 00:02:33.640
The story is set in the mythical city of Uranapolis,
where ho-hum humans and the angel-like Winged

00:02:33.650 --> 00:02:37.150
Tribe lived side-by-side, but not without
some hostility, of course.

00:02:37.150 --> 00:02:41.480
A war between the races led to the dominance
of the humans and the Winged Tribe losing

00:02:41.480 --> 00:02:42.900
its flying abilities.

00:02:42.900 --> 00:02:47.019
The movie picks up with an understandably
angry descendant of the most royal of the

00:02:47.019 --> 00:02:52.260
Winged Tribe, played by Simon Lam, going on
an adventure to locate the fabled Naga Pearls,

00:02:52.260 --> 00:02:54.360
which would destroy the humans once and for
all.

00:02:54.420 --> 00:02:58.420
Those pearls, however, accidentally wind up
in the possession of a human prince, constable,

00:02:58.420 --> 00:03:02.950
and thief, and they do everything they can
to keep them out of their enemy's hands, a

00:03:02.950 --> 00:03:07.670
process which involves epic battles and dazzling
fight and flight sequences that'll turn even

00:03:07.670 --> 00:03:10.000
the most jaded viewer into a fan for life.

00:03:10.780 --> 00:03:12.760
"Freeze, you jive-time suckas!"

00:03:13.120 --> 00:03:18.980
The only-in-the-'70s film genre known as "blaxploitation,"
hip, fight sequence-loaded action rides featuring

00:03:18.980 --> 00:03:24.469
predominantly African-American casts, is spoofed
in loving detail in Black Dynamite, a quirky,

00:03:24.469 --> 00:03:27.160
compelling, and extremely hilarious midnight
movie.

00:03:27.329 --> 00:03:32.140
Co-writer and star Michael Jai White shows
off his impressive martial arts skills, film

00:03:32.150 --> 00:03:37.469
history knowledge, and ability to crack the
perfect one-liners as the titular Black Dynamite,

00:03:37.469 --> 00:03:43.450
a one-man army and ex-CIA operative now set
on single-handedly fixing some problems both

00:03:43.450 --> 00:03:46.760
personal and societal by going after "The
Man."

00:03:46.760 --> 00:03:47.600
Who's the man?

00:03:47.780 --> 00:03:52.240
Pure evil, what with how he killed Black Dynamite's
brother, wants to get orphans addicted to

00:03:52.240 --> 00:03:56.799
drugs, and introduced an extra-strong malt
liquor into the black community that shrinks

00:03:56.800 --> 00:03:59.220
the, ahem, male reproductive organ.

00:03:59.440 --> 00:04:02.280
"Anaconda Malt Liquor gives you…

00:04:02.500 --> 00:04:04.040
Little Richard?"

00:04:05.500 --> 00:04:10.140
The plot is totally over the top in this adventure
inspired by Shaft and Superfly, except those

00:04:10.140 --> 00:04:14.390
flicks unfortunately didn't have any scenes
set on "Kung Fu Island," or mistakes thrown

00:04:14.390 --> 00:04:18.060
in on purpose to make the movie look like
a homemade labor of love.

00:04:18.060 --> 00:04:18.590
Dynamite!

